    "name": "id-artifact-serde-json (legacy, immutable)",
    "source": "pkgs/id/crates/id-sync/src/artifact.rs: signed_bytes() / SignedBody / SignedArtifact::build_signed / check_authenticity",
    "signed_bytes_definition": "serde_json::to_vec(SignedBody) — compact JSON, no whitespace; fields in declaration order author, seq, prev, kind, body, after; 'after' is OMITTED when empty (skip_serializing_if Vec::is_empty); body is a serde_json::Value whose object keys serialize in sorted (BTreeMap) order because preserve_order is not enabled; serde_json string escaping (quote, backslash, \\n, \\r, \\t short forms; other C0 controls as \\u00xx lowercase hex; non-ASCII emitted as raw UTF-8).",
    "hash": "hex lowercase SHA-256 over signed_bytes",
    "signature": "hex lowercase Ed25519 (ed25519-dalek, verify_strict on read) over signed_bytes",
    "doc_code_mismatch": "The signed_bytes doc comment claims the bytes are 'length-prefixed and domain-separated'; the implementation applies NO length prefixes and NO domain separation — it is exactly serde_json::to_vec(SignedBody). The verified bytes below are the immutable legacy behavior; the comment must not be treated as an interoperability claim.",
